Lamp colours follow the theme's own light/dark switch

The page draws the LED lamps in a dark-surface palette and switches to a light one when
the browser prefers light, unless the theme says dark through data-theme. Footstrap sets
data-theme; Vantage, the image's default theme, sets only data-darkmode. Under Vantage the
lamps therefore followed the operating system instead of the theme's toggle: a light
system with Vantage in dark mode drew the light palette on a dark card, and a dark system
with Vantage in light mode drew the near-black "off" lamp and the pale white lamp on a
light one.

data-darkmode is read as well, in both directions. Footstrap sets it beside data-theme, so
nothing changes under Footstrap. LuCI's Bootstrap sets data-darkmode too (from the system
for "Bootstrap", fixed for "BootstrapDark" and "BootstrapLight"), so its forced variants
now get the matching lamps as well.

Applies to: https://github.com/Pr0Luci/luci-app-cw-led.git @ a65586cf, after 0001.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

